Subject: Add unit tests for anisotropically scaled/rotated stroked rrects

This adds a test harness in CanvasTest.cpp (maybe worth pulling into
a separate header at some point) that lets you write a rendering
function targeting an SkCanvas*, and then returns a validation lambda
that processes the final SkBitmap. The harness handles running it on
CPU, Ganesh, and Graphite plus avoiding protected mode and dealilng
with the build defines.

Moves the ManyRect test into this harness as a proof of concept, and
then adds two new tests to cover the elliptical stroke rrect rendering
bugs that occurred when under an anisotropic scale and a 90 degree
rotation. I confirmed by undoing https://skia-review.git.corp.google.com/c/skia/+/1420157
that the first test catches the bug in the EllipseOp and the
second test catches the bug in EllipticalRRectOp.

